A||||16||Gold-86SE||Saturn Roadster Concept Unveiled||||1||
Z||000000||Gold-86SE||11-21-2001||03:30 PM||||<BR>From "My Saturn The Magazine" Fall 2001<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/saturn_roadster.jpg">  <P>Saturn' supercharged 180-horsepower "Sky" concept roadster certainly made an impression at Pebble Beach last August. But while most concept vehicles are designed to <I>test</I> public opinion, the Saturn Sky is the <I>result</I> of public opinion.<P>"It's a reaction to what young people told us they wanted," said Dave Smith Saturn's Brand Character Chief Designer. "They said they were looking for open air and room for their friends and their stuff, balanced with a sense of responsibility.  It tested so strongly, we just know this is a concept worth exploring."<P>"Here's a roadster done the Saturn way," added Jill Lajdziak, Vice President of Saturn Sales, Service and Marketing. "We've been offering a Different Kind of Car since our creation and now we are showing off a car the world has never seen - a stirring, open-air roadster that is an equal mix of fun and function."<P>The Saturn Sky is only a concept, but the ideas it has generated may be found in future Saturns. In this case, the Sky is definitely not the limit!<P>- - - - - - - - - - - - -<P>The weird thing is that my wife and I were at the Saturn dealership just yesterday and I ask one of the salesmen if there might be discussion of a future 2-seat roadster in the Saturn lineup, and lo-and-behold what do I receive in my mail today, "My Saturn The Magazine" answering my very question.  Maybe, just maybe, Saturn will wise up to the desire of folks like us to have a two-seater.<P>------------------<P>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Not So Fair Weather Driver)<BR>84 SE Automatic (Parts Car)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed   (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC Automatic (Blown Engine, seeking 2.5)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed   (Parts Car)<P>Edited to add the image, and correct spelling<p>[This message has been edited by Gold-86SE (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||11-21-2001||03:40 PM||||I saw a picture and some info on Saturn's website not too long ago.  I would almost start to get excited except that the writeup I saw sounded like it wasn't going to be much of a sports car and more of some kind of "Sport utility convertable" or something like that (my term).<P>It was also supposed to have its guages in the middle of the dash.  I ask, why does youthful have to equal guages in the middle of the dash??  (Read: Toyota Echo).  That alone would prevent me from buying it.  From a safety standpoint, I would also think it should be in front of the driver, not in front of the center armrest.  If they build one, maybe they will come to their senses!||||reg||1
